  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 257 AM MDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nSouthwest flow aloft continues and main impacts remain extreme\nheat with heat advisories in place for the Snake PLain, Eastern\nMagic Valley and southern hills. Will have scattered\nthunderstorms again in the southern hills and Snake River Plain\nwith strong thunderstorm outflow wind gusts expected. High\ntemperatures again near 100 in low elevations. The heat remains\nSunday with some drying expected. Have only minimal thunderstorm\ncoverage on Sunday in the eastern mountains. Long term grids\nhave minimal convection Tuesday and Wednesday in the eastern\nmountains but could see a bit more than what current grids have\nwith more activity possibly. Temperatures remain extremely hot\nthrough the entirety of next week. High temperatures remain in\nthe mid to upper 90s in lower elevations with some triple digits\npossible on many days. Mountain highs in the 80s to lower 90s.\nSo will be an extended period of extremely hot conditions\ncontinuing through the end of July.",
